,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498955127,"data":"Okay, so I need to solve this problem about Fibonacci numbers and some conditions on n. Let me read it again carefully.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498974139,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498979392,"data":"The problem says: There are N positive integers n strictly less than 10^101 such that n² + (n+1)² is a multiple of 5, but F_{n-1}² + F_n² is not. We need to find how many prime factors N has, counted with multiplicity. The answer should be an integer or NaN if no solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498985067,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498989326,"data":"First, let me parse the problem step by step.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498993774,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.498997436,"data":"We have two conditions on n:\n"}
