,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.499004933,"data":"1. n² + (n+1)² ≡ 0 mod 5\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.499008857,"data":"2. F_{n-1}² + F_n² ≢ 0 mod 5\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.499012767,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.499017819,"data":"And we need to count the number of such n less than 10^101, then factor that count N into its prime factors with multiplicity.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.499021987,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":673.499030372,"data":"Alright, so first step: figure out for which n the first condition holds. Then, for those n, check the second condition, and count how many satisfy both. Then factor that count.\n"}
